Fillets: the start of a blend that overflows on both sides of its edge,
rolling on the far edge of a narrow face on one side and touching a face
that continues the face of the edge tangentially on the other
(mitcad#121): e.g. the concave edge between a slanted side of a notch,
narrower than the rounding, and a straight side that runs on into a
round corner; the ball touches the corner and rolls on the slanted
side's far edge.

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSolOverflow (0011, 0013): each side's support
  moves on across the edge of its face that the section crosses. Where
  both sides moved at the same step and no ball touches the faces they
  reached, the side that moved last was taken for the one whose face the
  ball cannot touch (it went on over that face, or rolled on the edge
  before it). Where one of them moved onto a face that continues its face
  tangentially and the other across a sharp edge, the ball can only miss
  the face beyond the sharp edge: that side now rolls on that edge, and
  the other keeps the tangent face. Before, the tangent side went on over
  its face and no start was found (StartSol echec), or a start was found
  for the mirror image of the same notch only, by the order of the sides.
- BRepBlend_SurfRstLineBuilder::Perform: the start of a blend rolling on
  an edge (Appro) is solved from the given point. Where that solution
  touches the surface outside its face while its point on the edge lies
  inside the edge (the ball on another branch of the solution, e.g. on
  the far side of a cylinder), the section is solved again from points
  across the face (a 5 x 5 grid in its parameter box, the edge's parameter
  kept), and the first solution inside the face and on the edge, not
  leaving it, is the start. Before, the walk was not done (PerformSurf :
  Failed processing).
